From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:31:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nir/ir3: partially unroll bounded runtime loops on A8xx
 compute

Build a four-iteration body and a scalar tail for eligible runtime loops,
with overflow guards for the expanded induction range. Reject side effects,
barriers and subgroup operations, and bound loop cost and register demand.

Enable the pass for A8xx compute shaders and vectorize adjacent reads.
Adjust read scheduling and register headroom to keep the expanded loop
within the occupancy budget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
